.Dd 2026-10-24
.Dt asctob64 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm asctob64
.Nd a tool for encoding an ASCII string to Base64
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm asctob64
.Op Fl hu
.Ar string
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The command takes an ASCII
.Ar string
and returns a Base64-encoded equivalent string.
.Pp
The string should be enclosed in double quotes if it contains spaces.
.Pp
The
.Op -u 
option instructs the program to use URL-safe encoding rules when encoding the
string.
.Pp
The
.Op -h 
option simply instructs the program to display usage information. No conversion
is done.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
The program returns 0 on success, and 1 when an error occurred.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset
asctob64 "Hello, World!"
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr b64toasc 1 ,
.Xr b64 3
.Sh STANDARDS
.Pp
The program implements Base64 encoding and decoding according to the Internet
Engineering Task Force (IETF) Request For Comments (RFC) 4648 "The Base16,
Base32, and Base64 Data Encodings" standard.
.Pp
.Sh AUTHORS
.Pp
.An John Howie (Howie Consulting Inc.)
.Mt john@howieconsultinginc.com
.Pp
.Sh BUGS
There are no known bugs.
